INSERT INTO `mmf_composition` VALUES (1,2,9.00,65.20,0.00,1.90,23.90,'Fixed & demand deposits dominate (65.2%); collective investment schemes 23.9%; government securities 9.0%; cash 1.9%. Benchmark: 91-day T-Bill + 1.0%. Management fee 2.0%.','2025-08-31','Cytonn CMMF KES Fact Sheet, Aug 2025',0,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',6.00,2.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,'~65% in bank deposits — the fund\'s main engine. A mix of negotiated fixed deposits (indicative ~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with tier-1 and tier-2 Kenyan banks. Large balances let the fund negotiate above retail rates.','No corporate debt in the latest snapshot — the fund stays in government paper and bank deposits.','~2% in cash & near-cash for daily redemptions — current/settlement accounts and overnight placements (indicative ~3–6% p.a.). This is the liquidity buffer that lets you withdraw quickly.','~24% in regional / offshore or collective investment schemes — diversification beyond Kenya (East-Africa paper or units in other CIS). Adds breadth but introduces currency and cross-border considerations.','Cytonn\'s MMF holds 0% direct property — CMA rules forbid it. Cytonn Investments separately runs real-estate and high-yield products outside this fund; do not confuse the two.','No other asset classes beyond those listed.'),(2,26,44.68,55.32,0.00,0.00,0.00,'Deposits in financial institutions 55.32%; government securities 44.68%. Min initial KES 500,000. Note: as-of Apr 2024; verify against latest factsheet.','2024-04-30','GenAfrica MMF Fact Sheet, Apr 2024',0,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',26.00,12.68,6.00,0.00,0.00,'~55% in bank deposits — the fund\'s main engine. A mix of negotiated fixed deposits (indicative ~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with tier-1 and tier-2 Kenyan banks. Large balances let the fund negotiate above retail rates.','No corporate debt in the latest snapshot — the fund stays in government paper and bank deposits.','Minimal standalone cash; liquidity is met through maturing deposits and T-bills.','No offshore / regional exposure — a purely domestic Kenyan-shilling portfolio.','0% direct real estate. A CMA-regulated money market fund cannot legally hold property — it is restricted to short-term, high-quality, liquid instruments. Use the Other Assets page to track any property you own directly.','No other asset classes beyond those listed.'),(3,30007,30.00,50.00,12.00,8.00,0.00,'ESTIMATE. Diversified across government securities, bank deposits and commercial paper. Largest MMF by AUM (~KES 92.7B+); 2025 full-year return 13.4%. Verify exact split against latest SanlamAllianz factsheet.','2026-01-31','SanlamAllianz MMF Fact Sheet Jan 2026 (narrative); allocation estimated',1,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',17.00,8.00,5.00,0.00,0.00,'~50% in bank deposits — negotiated fixed deposits (~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with Kenyan banks, used for yield and liquidity.','~12% in corporate short-term debt — selective commercial paper / corporate notes at a modest spread over T-bills (indicative ~11–13% p.a.).','~8% in cash & near-cash for daily redemptions — current/settlement accounts and overnight placements (indicative ~3–6% p.a.). This is the liquidity buffer that lets you withdraw quickly.','No offshore / regional exposure — a purely domestic Kenyan-shilling portfolio.','0% direct real estate. A CMA-regulated money market fund cannot legally hold property — it is restricted to short-term, high-quality, liquid instruments. Use the Other Assets page to track any property you own directly.','No other asset classes beyond those listed.'),(4,19,30.00,45.00,15.00,10.00,0.00,'ESTIMATE. Invests in treasury bills, corporate notes, bank fixed deposits and bank call deposits. Verify exact split against latest OMIG factsheet.','2025-06-30','oldmutual.co.ke product page + OMIG factsheet (narrative); allocation estimated',1,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',17.00,8.00,5.00,0.00,0.00,'~45% in bank deposits — negotiated fixed deposits (~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with Kenyan banks, used for yield and liquidity.','~15% in corporate short-term debt — commercial paper and corporate notes from listed/large Kenyan issuers, typically priced at a 1–3% spread over T-bills (indicative ~11–14% p.a.). Higher reward, higher credit risk than government paper.','~10% in cash & near-cash for daily redemptions — current/settlement accounts and overnight placements (indicative ~3–6% p.a.). This is the liquidity buffer that lets you withdraw quickly.','No offshore / regional exposure — a purely domestic Kenyan-shilling portfolio.','0% direct property in the MMF. Old Mutual offers separate property and balanced funds; the MMF stays in cash-like instruments only.','No other asset classes beyond those listed.'),(5,14,35.00,50.00,8.00,7.00,0.00,'ESTIMATE. Invests in fixed deposits, government bonds, T-bills and cash. Fixed-principal investments >60% government + investment-grade corporate bonds. AUM ~KES 81.8B. Verify exact split against latest CIC factsheet.','2025-03-31','CIC MMF Fact Sheet Mar 2025 (narrative); allocation estimated',1,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',20.00,9.00,6.00,0.00,0.00,'~50% in bank deposits — negotiated fixed deposits (~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with Kenyan banks, used for yield and liquidity.','~8% in corporate short-term debt — selective commercial paper / corporate notes at a modest spread over T-bills (indicative ~11–13% p.a.).','~7% in cash & near-cash for daily redemptions — current/settlement accounts and overnight placements (indicative ~3–6% p.a.). This is the liquidity buffer that lets you withdraw quickly.','No offshore / regional exposure — a purely domestic Kenyan-shilling portfolio.','0% direct property in the MMF. CIC Asset Management runs a separate property fund; this MMF is cash-like only.','No other asset classes beyond those listed.'),(6,7,25.00,40.00,20.00,5.00,10.00,'ESTIMATE. Highest-yielding MMF in market per independent benchmarks. Regional/Africa breadth alongside government securities, banking instruments and corporate short-term debt. Verify exact split against latest Nabo factsheet.','2026-04-30','Nabo Capital (narrative) + Serrari/biznake benchmarks; allocation estimated',1,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',14.00,7.00,4.00,0.00,0.00,'~40% in bank deposits — negotiated fixed deposits (~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with Kenyan banks, used for yield and liquidity.','~20% in corporate short-term debt — commercial paper and corporate notes from listed/large Kenyan issuers, typically priced at a 1–3% spread over T-bills (indicative ~11–14% p.a.). Higher reward, higher credit risk than government paper.','~5% in cash & near-cash for daily redemptions — current/settlement accounts and overnight placements (indicative ~3–6% p.a.). This is the liquidity buffer that lets you withdraw quickly.','~10% in regional / offshore or collective investment schemes — diversification beyond Kenya (East-Africa paper or units in other CIS). Adds breadth but introduces currency and cross-border considerations.','0% direct real estate. A CMA-regulated money market fund cannot legally hold property — it is restricted to short-term, high-quality, liquid instruments. Use the Other Assets page to track any property you own directly.','No other asset classes beyond those listed.'),(7,4,20.00,55.00,18.00,7.00,0.00,'ESTIMATE. High-yield independent fund. Typically heavy on bank deposits and corporate short-term debt with government securities for liquidity. Verify exact split against latest Etica factsheet.','2026-04-30','Etica Capital (narrative); allocation estimated',1,'2026-06-22 13:37:32','2026-06-22 15:26:21',12.00,5.00,3.00,0.00,0.00,'~55% in bank deposits — the fund\'s main engine. A mix of negotiated fixed deposits (indicative ~9–12% p.a.) and call deposits (~6–9% p.a.) with tier-1 and tier-2 Kenyan banks. Large balances let the fund negot